\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Consciousness Detection Results: Empirical ch$_2$ measurements across different consciousness states. Shows clear separation between: unconscious (ch$_2$ $< 0.2$), drowsy (ch$_2$ $\approx 0.4$), normal waking (ch$_2$ $\approx 0.6$), focused attention (ch$_2$ $\approx 0.8$), and peak consciousness (ch$_2$ $\geq 0.95$). Validates theoretical predictions.}}{696}{figure.Alph0.15}%
